Notebook[{Cell["Start here", "Title"], Cell["This notebook loads the package, \
checks that every program is installed, and runs the first process.  Evaluate \
the cells one after the other (Shift+Enter).  The calculations themselves are \
in the notebooks under Processes/; open them to read and evaluate each step."\
, "Text"], Cell["1. Load the package", "Section"], 
  Cell[
   "Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"FeynFacet\", \
\"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["2. Check the installation", "Section"], 
  Cell["Every row must show a location (and a version where the program has \
one).  A row marked NOT FOUND shows what to install; after installing, \
evaluate the cell again.  If a program is installed but not found, give its \
path in Paths.wl (see Paths.example.wl).", "Text"], 
  Cell["CheckInstallation[]", "Input"], 
  Cell["3. Run the lepton-quark process", "Section"], 
  Cell["RunSteps evaluates the five step files of Processes/LeptonQuark in \
order, each in a fresh kernel: FeynArts amplitudes, the FeynCalc algebra, the \
Kira reduction and master integrals, and the unpolarized and polarized \
assemblies, which end by comparing with the published coefficients.  About \
five minutes.  Use \"FORM\" or \"Tracer\" as the second argument for the \
other algebra routes.", "Text"], 
  Cell["RunSteps[\"LeptonQuark\", \"FeynCalc\"]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"Processes\", \
\"LeptonQuark\", \"Results\", \"FeynCalc\", \
\"Polarized.wl\"}]][\"Coefficients\"] // TableForm", "Input"], 
  Cell["The results are now in Processes/LeptonQuark/Results/FeynCalc/.  The \
step notebooks are in Processes/LeptonQuark/:", "Text"], 
  Cell["If[$FrontEnd =!= Null, SystemOpen[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"Processes\", \"LeptonQuark\"}]]]", "Input"], Cell["4. Run the TMD process", 
   "Section"], Cell["The NLO TMD beam-function matching coefficients and the \
soft function (Processes/TMD), generated from a FeynArts model in which \
Wilson lines and operators are fields; about one minute.  Regenerated \
diagrams are written to Processes/TMD/Results/figures/.", "Text"], 
  Cell["RunSteps[\"TMD\", \"FeynCalc\"]", "Input"], 
  Cell["5. The other processes", "Section"], Cell["The off-diagonal lepton \
channels l q -> g + X and l g -> q + X (Processes/LeptonOffDiagonal, about \
four minutes, compared with Hinderer, Schlegel and Vogelsang), the transverse \
spin transfer l q -> q + X for the Collins asymmetry with its resolved-photon \
Born table (Processes/Collins, about ten minutes, compared with the paper), \
the table of all 2 -> 2 Born channels (Processes/PartonicBorn, eight minutes) \
and the 16 proton-proton classes (Processes/Hadronic, one class at a time, \
minutes to hours; compared with the reference codes) run the same way:", 
   "Text"], Cell["RunSteps[\"LeptonOffDiagonal\", \"FeynCalc\"]", "Input"], 
  Cell["RunSteps[\"Collins\", \"FeynCalc\"]", "Input"], 
  Cell["RunSteps[\"PartonicBorn\", \"FeynCalc\"]", "Input"], 
  Cell["A proton-proton class is selected with the class variable of its step \
files (the fourth argument of RunSteps overrides it); the Born table above \
must exist.  Class 2 (q q' -> g + X, no virtual correction) takes about ten \
minutes, class 1 about twenty:", "Text"], 
  Cell["RunSteps[\"Hadronic\", \"FeynCalc\", All, \"class=2\"]", "Input"]}, 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
